  "verified_on": "2026-09-05",
  "entries": [
    {
      "entry": 0,
      "root": "Čop, Čop-gân",
      "verdict": "plausible",
      "modern_form": "Middle Persian čōb 'wood, stick' (Pahl. cwp), with its derivative čōbagān / čōbgān (Pahl. cwpk'n', cwpygʾn'; MacKenzie reads čaw(la)gān) 'curved polo-stick, the game of polo' — not an Old Persian word",
      "note": "The etymon itself is real and the gloss is right: MacKenzie, A Concise Pahlavi Dictionary p.24 'čōb [cwp | N ~] wood, stick', and p.23 'čaw(la)gān [cwpkʾn' | Ar. sawlajān, N čawgān] (curved) polo-stick; polo'; Nyberg, Manual of Pahlavi II p.59 'čōwčgān [cwpygʾn'] the stick used in playing polo … NP čaugān; Arab. lw. saulajān'. What is wrong is the language label: there is no Old Persian *čub-. Kent's Old Persian lexicon has no such stem (OP for 'wood' is dāru-, DSf 41), and Horn no.448 himself labels the older form 'phlv. čōp', i.e. Pahlavi/Middle Persian. So the root box should read 'Middle Persian' (or simply 'Persian'), not 'Old Persian'. The old attempt to attach čōb to Sanskrit kṣupa- 'bush' is rejected by Horn ('Lässt sich lautlich nicht mit skr. kṣupa- … vermitteln') and Wiktionary likewise says 'further connections outside Indo-Iranian uncertain'. Two further page-level observations: (a) HRN:99 covers čōb (no.448) but čōgān is no.449 on p.100; (b) the Greek box on the printed page really is empty — the extraction is faithful (see node #6).",
      "note_fa": "ریشهٔ این مدخل واقعی است اما برچسب زبانی آن نادرست است. کهن‌ترین صورت گواهی‌شده فارسی میانه (پهلوی) čōb «چوب، چوبدست» است (مکنزی، فرهنگ کوچک پهلوی، ص ۲۴: cwp) و مشتق آن čōbagān/čōbgān «چوگان» (مکنزی ص ۲۳؛ نیبرگ ج۲ ص ۵۹: cwpygʾn'). در پارسی باستان چنین ستاکی گواهی نشده است؛ کنت در واژه‌نامهٔ پارسی باستان تنها dāru- «چوب» را دارد. هرن نیز (شمارهٔ ۴۴۸، ص ۹۹) صورت کهن‌تر را «پهلوی čōp» می‌نامد، نه پارسی باستان. پیوند دادن čōb به سنسکریت kṣupa- «بوته» را هرن به دلیل ناسازگاری آوایی رد می‌کند و ویکی‌واژه نیز آن را نامطمئن می‌داند. بنابراین ادعای معنایی نورایی درست است ولی «پارسی باستان» باید به «فارسی میانه» اصلاح شود.",
      "sources": [
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%DA%86%D9%88%D8%A8",
        "https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/%DA%86%D9%88%DA%AF%D8%A7%D9%86"
      ],
      "ref_check": [
        {"ref": "HRN:99", "status": "partial", "note": "Horn, Grundriss p.99 no.448 (HRN.txt leaf 120): '448. čōb \"Holz\". phlv. čōp \"Holz\" (Guj. Ab.); kurd. čō, siw; bal. LW. čōp; wa. čōpk, sar. čūb.' — it supports the word and gloss but labels the ancestor Pahlavi, not Old Persian; and čōgān is no.449 on p.100, not p.99."}
      ],
      "consulted": [
        {"src": "PHD", "where": "p.24 s.v. čōb (PHD.txt leaf 45)", "stance": "supports", "note": "'čōb [cwp | N ~] wood, stick.' — the Middle Persian etymon exactly as Nourai's root, but Middle not Old Persian."},
        {"src": "NYB", "where": "Part II Glossary p.59 (NYB_vol2_glossary.txt leaf 67)", "stance": "supports", "note": "'čōwčgān [cwpygʾn'] the stick used in playing polo …; the game of polo itself. — NP čaugān; Arab. lw. saulajān-; Fraenkel, Aram. Fremdw. 291; Horn, NP Et. no. 4[4]9 and Hübschmann' — the Pahlavi spelling cwpygʾn' shows the word is built on cwp = čōb."},
        {"src": "KNT", "where": "Kent, Old Persian, Lexicon and §86 (KNT.txt)", "stance": "contradicts", "note": "No stem čub-/čōb- in Kent's OP lexicon; the OP word for wood is dāru- ('asā dāruv', DSf 41). Nothing supports an Old Persian label."},
        {"src": "HUB", "where": "Persische Studien (HUB.txt), grep čōb / čōgān / čaugān", "stance": "silent", "note": "no hit in the OCR of Hübschmann's Persische Studien (Mo'in's footnote cites 'هوبشمان ۴۴' for čōgān, but that page is not retrievable in this scan)."},
        {"src": "ARY", "where": "Aryanpur, ARY_pages.txt, grep چوب / چوگان", "stance": "silent", "note": "no headword چوب or چوگان; the word occurs only inside other entries (e.g. 'چوبدستی')."}
      ],
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "lang": "Persian",
          "words": "čŭb «چوب»; čowgân «چوگان»",
          "verdict": "confirmed",
          "derivation": "چوب čūb continues Middle Persian čōb (Pahlavi spelling cwp, MacKenzie p.24) with the regular New Persian raising of Middle Persian ō to ū (cf. rōz > rūz, sōz > sūz); Horn no.448 gives the same chain with the dialect cognates kurd. čō, bal. čōp, sar. čūb. چوگان čowgān is a derivative of the same čōb: Middle Persian čōbagān / čōbgān (Pahl. cwpkʾn', cwpygʾn'), i.e. čōb 'stick' + the denominal suffix -agān, whence loss of the intervocalic -b- gives čōgān > NP čowgān. Borhan-e Qate' still carries the older headword چوبگان beside چوگان, which is direct evidence for the derivation from چوب. From the Sasanian court game the word passed into Arabic as صولجان ṣawlajān (MacKenzie p.23 'Ar. sawlajān'; Mo'in s.v. صولجان '[معرّب چوگان]') and into Byzantine Greek as τζυκάνιον (see node #6). So both words of the node, and the arrow čōb → čowgān, are correct.",
